	// ---------- Fish Descriptions ----------
	// ES - fish
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Aideen": "Un tel rouge flamboyant n'est pas rare pour un betta, mais cette nageoire arrière n'a rien de commun.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Beatrice": "Un cousin éloigné des carpes, semblerait-il. Il dégage un parfum de printemps.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Corwin": "Cette drôle de créature ronde ne semble pas apprécier d'être comparée à une certaine possession de pirate.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Dale": "D'étranges appendices à l'aspect métallique semblent traverser son corps.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Edith": "Un petit poisson violet tout mignon, dont la présence annonce un printemps bien fleuri !",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Eloise": "Ça sonnait comme une fausse piste, mais non, il y avait bien un poisson ici!",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Ethan": "Il est si petit, vous pouvez à peine le tenir entre vos mains.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Eyvind": "Ces branches sont si jolies, presque dorée, mais ne luisant pas. Pour autant, vous ne devriez pas y toucher.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Jacob": "Ce poisson calme n'apprécie guère toute l'attention que vous lui portez. Arrêtez de le tapoter !",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Jade": "A nudibranch in a tide pool is nothing unusual. What is however is how intensely it is looking at you",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Jasper": "OK now, a nudibranch in the mines, that's a bit more unusual. Especially one clamped to some rusty old artifact.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Jessie": "Just looking at this fish is making you smile. You can almost feel how it want to smile too.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Josephine": "These fish usually bask under the moon. This one doesn't seem to care about the sunlight.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Juliet": "An energetic discus, decidedly far from any other kind of discus. How did it get here?",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Kataryna": "Its name comes from the amount of food it take away, but it doesn't actually seem to eat it itself, instead feeding it to other and waiting for an opportunity... for what? It's just a fish.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Keanu": "A large flat fish, who seem to enjoy letting the currents take it away.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Kennedy": "This little fish doesn't seem to like how you fished it out of the comfort of this plush. Too bad for it.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Lexi": "You knew to expect peculiar things in this cave, but not a weirdly wide and green nudibranch.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Luma": "It's so round! And tiny! And bright!",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Michael": "How the hell did it hid in the rug fibers? You have no idea, but you caught it anyway.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Oliver": "It doesn't seem very happy that you pulled it out of its home. Guess it'll need to find new friends in a tank.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Rosa": "No no, this is not a hat, just a very weirdly shaped dorsal fin. But it does look like a hat...",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Stella": "This very triangular fish sports a brightly pink dorsal fin.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Tristan": "It reminds you of something... Oh yeah, a lingcod!",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Victoria": "You thought it was a coin? Ha! You got got by the goldseeker!",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Vivienne": "Its ventral fins rattle, like pages of a book.",
	// ES - crabpot
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Abyss": "The way it looks at you... Is it friendly, or does it want to eat your soul?",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.BaronMunchington": "It so soft and fluffy! Although, if this appendix could stop hitting your hand whenever you try to touch it...",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Cameron": "A big coral-looking creature, with an uneasy smirk-like coloration on its front.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.CaptainRoderick": "This creature like to curl up this specific way to lure others into thinking it is an inert object.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Gremlin": "The two triangular appendices on its head happily move around when you look at it.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Happy": "This time you really though you caught some gold ore in your crab pot...",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.LadySheba": "It looks like it enter the trap to scrap for food inside the pot.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.LittleGruff": "An aquatic creature, shaped like a duck, with a goat head... Which myth did you enter this time?",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Pepper": "Despite all your best effort, you can't hold it in your hand. Not because it's small or slippery, but because it won't stop moving!",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Richie": "It would have been a much more believable stick if not for all these colors.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.TheEmperess": "A very royal-looking fish... Or should you say duck-looking royal-looking fish?",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.TheEmperor": "This duck-looking fish has some strange aura to it, almost as if it was at the top of the world.",
	"NPCFish.Desc.EastScarp.Valkyrie": "It looks a bit scary, but it's actually very friendly! And also very still.",

	// ---------- Note Titles ----------
	"NPCFish.Hint.Title.EastScarpSoggyNote1": "New species in the 'Scarp",
	"NPCFish.Hint.Title.EastScarpSoggyNote2": "A wider spread",
	"NPCFish.Hint.Title.EastScarpSoggyNote3": "An EVEN wider spread",
	"NPCFish.Hint.Title.EastScarpSoggyNote4": "They are everywhere",
	"NPCFish.Hint.Title.EastScarpSoggyNote5": "Haunted inn?",
	"NPCFish.Hint.Title.EastScarpSoggyNote6": "Phenomenons in the Suburbs",
	"NPCFish.Hint.Title.EastScarpSoggyNote7": "Revised scope",
	
	// ---------- Hint ----------
	"NPCFish.Hint.EastScarpSoggyNote1": "The town has always been home to endemic fish, but there have been a recently influx of curious fish here too, like in Pelican Town. Two in the river, another two in the bay - plus one in the tidepools! - and a last one in the pond. I've also heard someone talked about another one in the cove too, in fall.",
	"NPCFish.Hint.EastScarpSoggyNote2": "The town isn't the only place saddled by the curse of fish. A pair of fish have been spotted in the crossing, in fall and summer. In these same seasons, another two were noticed in the orchard.",
	"NPCFish.Hint.EastScarpSoggyNote3": "Even the most unusual locations seem to have been touched.^^Some talk of a strange coral, under the snow, in the mountains...^^Two curious ones, in a mysterious cave, under the harsh sun...",
	"NPCFish.Hint.EastScarpSoggyNote4": "There was already a lot of curious new fish in this town, but now it looks like there is even more? Someone mentioned splashing noise at the bottom of the well, last summer, and a strange rumour runs about scales spotted in the bush cluster near the lighthouse...",
	"NPCFish.Hint.EastScarpSoggyNote5": "So many strange things have been happening in the inn!^The showers have been gurgling all winter, the barrels emptying faster than usual last spring, and the entryway carpet seems to always be wet in fall...^Do you think there is a ghost there?",
	"NPCFish.Hint.EastScarpSoggyNote6": "I feel like I'm going crazy... First, the couch in the thrift store's been wet the whole fall, and now I'm seeing fish jump in the flower parcels?? Maybe the cold is turning me mad.",
	"NPCFish.Hint.EastScarpSoggyNote7": "Our initial touring of Pelican Town wasn't enough it seems. A new one has been spotted in the mines, two in the town river, one in the ocean, and a last one in between.",

	// ---------- Trophy ----------
	"NPCFish.EastScarp.Trophy.Name": "East Scarp collection Trophy",
	"NPCFish.EastScarp.Trophy.Mail.Content": "A true menagerie in this collection, don't you think?^I mean, in a way they are all fish - or, well, living creatures inhabiting water -, so all collections have been menageries...^^Anyway.^^All this to say: congrats! Here's your reward.^Take care of it, I want to see it shine through your window.^^- A friend.",
	"NPCFish.EastScarp.Trophy.Mail.Title": "NPC Fish East Scarp collection complete"
}